# Check every text file out with LF line endings on every platform.
#
# Vite's SSR transform (used by vitest) only recognises a leading shebang when
# the line ends in LF; a CRLF checkout (Windows core.autocrlf=true) leaves the
# "#!" line in the middle of the transformed module and every test that
# imports the script fails with "Invalid or unexpected token". Shell scripts
# and lockfiles are just as sensitive. Pinning LF makes a Windows clone behave
# exactly like CI (ubuntu-latest).
* text=auto eol=lf
